# "Whenever this creature enters or attacks, put a blight counter on it. Then for each blight counter on it, each opponent
# loses 4 life unless that player sacrifices a nonland permanent of their choice or discards a card." Show and Tell puts
# Rottenmouth Viper onto the battlefield for Bot1 and Ornithopter for Bot2: it enters with no counter, gets one, and Bot2
# sacrifices the Ornithopter rather than lose 4 life. On turn 3 it attacks: a second counter, and Bot2 answers twice - it
# loses 4 life for the first, and discards a Lightning Bolt for the second (CR 608.2c: "unless" is the player's choice).
# The Viper's 6 combat damage follows: 20 - 4 - 6 = 10.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Show and Tell
Rottenmouth Viper
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Lightning Bolt x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Show and Tell.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Rottenmouth Viper)
Bot2.Choose(Ornithopter)
Bot2.Modes(Sacrifice a nonland permanent)
Bot2.Choose(Ornithopter)
? Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
? Bot2.Life = 20
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Rottenmouth Viper > Bot2)
Bot2.Modes(Lose 4 life)
Bot2.Modes(Discard a card)
Bot2.Choose(Lightning Bolt)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot2.Life = 10
Bot1.Battlefield.Rottenmouth Viper.Counters.Blight = 2
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt; Ornithopter
Bot2.Hand.Count = 6
